p Nitrous makes programming more enjoyable and programmers and teams more productive. As a developer evangelist, you will interact with programmers of all experience levels to educate them on Nitrous' most powerful features, and use customer feedback to continually improve the product.

p We at Nitrous are looking for a developer evangelist with boundless energy who loves to travel, connect with new people, and is obsessed with new technology and improving how developers work.

h3 Responsibilities

ul
  li Speaking at events to promote the value of Nitrous
  li Writing Call for Papers and Abstracts to submit to developer conferences
  li Traveling to conferences and representing the company
  li Writing tutorials about how to use Nitrous with different technologies
  li Creating "how-to" videos, webinars and other introduction videos
  li Collecting and sharing developer feedback for Nitrous product improvement

h3 Requirements

ul
  li Excellent written and verbal communication skills, bonus points for technical writing
  li Experience with public speaking to large audiences, specifically on technical topics
  li Proven track record of relevant development
  li Strong social skills
  li Willingness to travel

p To apply, please provide the following:

ul
  li Github Profile with code you've written
  li Links to blog and/or videos of talks
  li Links to community profiles like Twitter, Hacker News, Stack Overflow, Reddit, etc...
  li How you want to improve development


